{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/158343-smoky-mountain-darkness-a-homebrew-take-on-cwod","id":158343,"title":"Smoky Mountain Darkness: A Homebrew Take on cWoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-03T15:27:40-07:00","id":158343,"title":"Smoky Mountain Darkness: A Homebrew Take on cWoD","content":"Hey guys, as some of you may know, I'm not a fan of personal horror. I can take it in small doses or when a really skilled ST handles it well, but it's not my cup of tea. If you guys like it, that's cool by me. This isn't one of <i>those </i>threads, I assure you. However, this is a thread for the development of my own homebrew setting for a World of Darkness that is neither Gothic nor Punk, nor oriented in personal horror, but instead in Action-Adventure and Modern Fantasy. This is Smoky Mountain Darkness.<br /> <br /> And no, I'm not asking how to remove personal horror and add in action-adventure in CWOD, I have learned how to do that, no, this is a setting construction thread. Just want that to be clear, just to be safe.<br /> <br /> Smoky Mountain Darkness is an alternate take on Classic World of Darkness focused on dark action-adventure tales and pulp modern fantasy. It is named so because the default setting I'm using in my inaugural games is the Central Appalachian region of the Southeastern and Mid-Atlantic United States, specifically around the states of Tennessee, Virginia, West Virginia, Kentucky, North Carolina, and Pennsylvania. It's a bit of a misnomer as it covers not just the Smoky Mountains but also the Blue Ridge Mountains, the Shenandoah Valley, the Alleghenies, and the Coalfields, but Smoky Mountain Darkness just sounds cool. Naturally, ST's who wish to use the setting of Smoky Mountain Darkness can set it in other regions of the world as well.<br /> <br /> This is a World of Darkness that runs on Rule of Cool, a World of Darkness full of katanas, mystery, adventure, intrigue, action, and dark fantasy. One that's more Iron Maiden and less Sisters of Mercy (both equally great bands by the way, but completely different in tone and style, much like Smoky Mountain Darkness and the canonical Classic World of Darkness are equally great but in different ways). There's some key differences between the canonical World of Darkness and Smoky Mountain Darkness though.<br /> <br /> Either way, everything here is property of CCP/White Wolf, Capcom, and various anime companies. I own nothing.<br /> <br /> <b>The following game lines are the core of Smoky Mountain Darkness</b><br /> <br /> Vampire: The Masquerade<br /> Werewolf: The Apocalypse<br /> Mage: The Ascension<br /> Changeling: The Lost (replaces Dreaming)<br /> Street Fighter: The Storytelling Game<br /> Senshi: The Merchandising (A humorous though well-crafted fan game importing Sailor Moon and other 90's anime into the World of Darkness, and one of my personal favorites)<br /> <br /> <b>The following game lines are non-existent in Smoky Mountain Darkness</b><br /> <br /> Demon: The Fallen<br /> Kindred of the East<br /> Hunter: The Reckoning<br /> Orpheus<br /> Changeling: The Dreaming<br /> <br /> <b>These game lines are loosely canon in a &quot;broad strokes&quot; sort of way in Smoky Mountain Darkness</b><br /> <br /> Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> Mummy: The Resurrection<br /> <br /> In addition to Kuei-Jin being replaced by Cainites, while Fallen and Imbued being erased out completely, the entirety of the original metaplot is removed from Smoky Mountain Darkness. So no Week of Nightmares, Avatar Storms, Red Stars, Sixth Great Maelstroms, or Independent Gangrel to be found here. In addition the Judeo-Christian/Abrahamic creation story is NOT the 100% canonically correct origin story in Smoky Mountain Darkness like it was in the canonical World of Darkness. Instead it's just a theory. Demon: The Fallen is given the axe and as for the Caine theory? That's all it is, a theory. There certainly was a progenitor vampire, but the idea of that progenitor being Caine was simply the predominant theory among Western Kindred due to the influence of Christianity in the Western World and Islam in the Middle East. The Antediluvians certainly exist but the name Antediluvian is strictly a Western one. East Asian Cainites refer to the Third Generation as the Yama Kings and African Kindred have their own name for the Third Generation.<br /> <br /> The starting setting is a city in the Appalachian Mountains, I'm personally leaning towards either the combined metropolitan areas of either Knoxville, Tennessee or alternately, Roanoke, Virginia. I've frequently visited the former and currently reside in the latter (and have for seven years now). Either way, I'm seeking to build the opening setting with your help, Onyx Path Forums. Personally, I'm leaning more towards Knoxville because the combined metro area is larger (as it covers Knoxville, Knox County, Morristown, Gatlinburg, Pigeon Forge, and Sevierville, among other places), but Roanoke could be the second place on the list.<br /> <br /> I want Knoxville to be to Smoky Mountain Darkness what Chicago was to 1st Edition and 2nd Edition Masquerade. I want to build a living, breathing city with detailed NPC's of Vampires, Werewolves, Magi, Changelings, Street Fighters, and Senshi. And I'm wondering if anyone here is willing to collaborate with me on this endeavor of creating the inaugural setting of Smoky Mountain Darkness, titled <b>Knoxville by Night.</b><br /> <br /> Any help or feedback would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 06-03-2014, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T05:36:55-07:00","id":158937,"title":"","content":"Lakeshore Mental Asylum<br /> <br /> This place is rich in history and &quot;spooky&quot; factor as is. It could be a good haunt for various types of supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Sunsphere<br /> <br /> This thing was built &quot;to scale&quot; of the sun. This seems like an interesting place to conduct some magickal research, or perhaps to hide a laboratory or portal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T08:14:53-07:00","id":159063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/158343-smoky-mountain-darkness-a-homebrew-take-on-cwod?p=158937#post158937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lakeshore Mental Asylum<br /> <br /> This place is rich in history and &quot;spooky&quot; factor as is. It could be a good haunt for various types of supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Sunsphere<br /> <br /> This thing was built &quot;to scale&quot; of the sun. This seems like an interesting place to conduct some magickal research, or perhaps to hide a laboratory or portal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are great ideas, I was thinking the Sunsphere would be an awesome place for a chantry of Mages to take root. I'll look more into Lakeshore Mental Asylum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:57:21-07:00","id":159162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/158343-smoky-mountain-darkness-a-homebrew-take-on-cwod?p=159063#post159063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both are great ideas, I was thinking the Sunsphere would be an awesome place for a chantry of Mages to take root. I'll look more into Lakeshore Mental Asylum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a small chantry who are experimenting with the &quot;Origin Point&quot; of the Universe. Perhaps the Sunsphere is part of an elaborate ritual to &quot;move&quot; the origin point to our very own Sol, thus giving them a way to affect any point in the Universe from their very own lab. They might be setting up other spheres around town in scaled distances (based on the scale of the Sunsphere) to create a model of the entire solar system.<br /> <br /> Perhaps as they set up each sphere and tie it to the real planet (and thus the Shard Realm), it begins to create subtle and pervasive effects on the areas around it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Bijou Theatre sounds like the perfect place for a Toreador Prince.<br /> <br /> <i>In 1815 Humes began constructing a hotel and tavern, which was to be named the \u201cThomas Humes House.\u201d Humes unfortunately died in September 1816 shortly before the construction was completed. The building was finally completed in the July of 1817. It was described as a &quot;large and elegant building of three stories and fifteen rooms&quot; and its first occupant was a man named Archibald Rhea. </i><br /> <br /> Thomas Humes certainly died, but he was also perfectly capable of enjoying the building for the next 198 years (assuming 2014). Archibald Rhea was a trusted friend who became Thomas's first ghoul and liason with the living world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> UT Knoxville has an impressive &quot;Genome Science&quot; program. This is obviously a front for Progenitor research and recruitment. I imagine the entire university is overrun by Technocrats. There is likely a Kindred spy among them, possibly Brujah. That would be a veritable powder-keg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":2211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","user":"SixFootChicken","date":". 06-04-2014, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T13:49:22-07:00","id":159337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/158343-smoky-mountain-darkness-a-homebrew-take-on-cwod?p=159162#post159162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe a small chantry who are experimenting with the &quot;Origin Point&quot; of the Universe. Perhaps the Sunsphere is part of an elaborate ritual to &quot;move&quot; the origin point to our very own Sol, thus giving them a way to affect any point in the Universe from their very own lab. They might be setting up other spheres around town in scaled distances (based on the scale of the Sunsphere) to create a model of the entire solar system.<br /> <br /> Perhaps as they set up each sphere and tie it to the real planet (and thus the Shard Realm), it begins to create subtle and pervasive effects on the areas around it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Bijou Theatre sounds like the perfect place for a Toreador Prince.<br /> <br /> <i>In 1815 Humes began constructing a hotel and tavern, which was to be named the \u201cThomas Humes House.\u201d Humes unfortunately died in September 1816 shortly before the construction was completed. The building was finally completed in the July of 1817. It was described as a &quot;large and elegant building of three stories and fifteen rooms&quot; and its first occupant was a man named Archibald Rhea. </i><br /> <br /> Thomas Humes certainly died, but he was also perfectly capable of enjoying the building for the next 198 years (assuming 2014). Archibald Rhea was a trusted friend who became Thomas's first ghoul and liason with the living world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> UT Knoxville has an impressive &quot;Genome Science&quot; program. This is obviously a front for Progenitor research and recruitment. I imagine the entire university is overrun by Technocrats. There is likely a Kindred spy among them, possibly Brujah. That would be a veritable powder-keg.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like these ideas, keep 'em coming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}